messages:
maria: Heads-up — a customer hit a weird failure on Cloudflare Workers after upgrading to SDK v0.9.0. 415 Unsupported Media Type when we retry auth requests. Anyone seen this?

sahil: I saw something similar in e2e earlier. CF Workers handles Request/Headers differently than node fetch. When we clone and re-attach headers on retry we end up sending duplicate Authorization sometimes.

ben: Minimal repro I made:
```js
// worker.js
addEventListener('fetch', e => {
  const req = e.request;
  // our SDK does a retry that clones the Request
  const r1 = new Request(req);
  r1.headers.append('authorization', req.headers.get('authorization'));
  // fetch(r1) -> downstream errors with 415 on some origins
});
```

maria: The customer stack (NGINX + auth proxy) rejects the duplicate header. On node it was fine due to header normalization.

karen: This matches older notes: CF's Request/Headers flattening means append + passing Request can create multi-value headers. Also some CDNs interpret duplicate auth headers differently.

maria: Another wrinkle: our retry wrapper sets Authorization in both the Request object and the fetch init headers. That double-set is the root cause in their case.

sahil: Proposed quick fix: when retrying, build a fresh Request with a single headers object constructed from existing values (no append). E.g.
```js
const auth = req.headers.get('authorization');
const headers = new Headers();
if (auth) headers.set('authorization', auth);
const retryReq = new Request(req.url, {
  method: req.method,
  headers,
  body: await req.clone().arrayBuffer(),
});
```
This ensures single-value header on Workers.

ben: Typings FYI: our ESM build pulled in `import type { Readable } from 'stream'` which makes TypeScript try to resolve node types for consumers on Cloudflare (bad). For edge builds we should only expose web types (ReadableStream).

maria: Agreed. We need an explicit edge entrypoint in package.json ("exports"/"browser") and a separate tsconfig for edge that uses lib: ["webworker", "es2021"] so consumers in Workers don't pick up node types.

karen: Also add a runtime check in the SDK that prefers `globalThis.fetch` + `globalThis.ReadableStream` paths for edge. Feature-detect instead of package-level assumptions.

maria: Can someone add a tiny sample app under samples/edge-auth-dup that reproduces the issue in Miniflare CI? It should exercise the retry path and show header duplication. Keep it tiny.

sahil: I'll take it. I'll also open a PR with two commits: (1) runtime-safe retry implementation (no append), (2) edge tsconfig + new export entry. Will include unit + Miniflare integration test.

ben: For changelog: call it "fix(workers): avoid duplicating Authorization on retries" and mention typings fix in a separate line.

maria: Also add a note to the migration guide: if you previously relied on Node header normalization, inline the change for edge.

ci-bot: Created ticket RN-4321: "CF Workers: prevent duplicate Authorization on SDK retry; add edge export + typing fix" and linked repo: https://git.internal/redwood/rn/4321

maria: awesome, thx. assigning to @sahil, please ping when the sample is live. :thumbsup:

sahil: will do — aiming for a PR today.

karen: small follow-up: add a lint rule to forbid `headers.append('authorization', ...)` in retry code paths to prevent regressions.

maria: great idea. adding that to the PR checklist.
